// "Build with Claude AI" worker handler — SAFE, plan-then-approve.
//
// Two phases, driven by ClaudeBuild.approved:
//   1. PLAN  (approved=false): ask Claude — with the OWNER'S effective key — for
//      an ordered JSON array of non-destructive shell commands. Store it to
//      ClaudeBuild.plan and set AWAITING_APPROVAL. NOTHING is executed.
//   2. EXECUTE (approved=true): run each approved command over SSH, enforcing a
//      denylist, a per-command timeout, and a hard command cap. Append output to
//      ClaudeBuild.log, then set DONE (or FAILED on error). Never runs a command
//      that was not part of the approved plan.
//
// This handler is wired into worker/index.ts's `handlers` map by the
// orchestrator (see INTEGRATION NEEDED in the final report):
//   import { claudeBuild } from "./claude";
//   CLAUDE_BUILD: claudeBuild,

